<title>EGYPT: Egypt raises cotton export prices for four grades.</title>
<headline>Egypt raises cotton export prices for four grades.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-12-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian exporters raised export prices for four grades of cotton and kept prices for the three remaining grades unchanged, the Alexandria Cotton Exporters Association (Alcotexa) said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The association said prices for Giza 76, Giza 70 and Giza 77 were raised by two centilibres (U.S. cents per lb). Giza 75 prices were increased by one centilibre.</p>
<p>The prices in centilibres (valid until 2200 GMT December 28) are:</p>
<p>	     FG/EX    FG+1/4     FG     FG-1/4    G/FG    G+3/8</p>
<p> Giza 76   178.0    172.0    166.0    160.0    154.0    151.0</p>
<p> Giza 70   171.0    165.0    159.0    153.0    147.0    144.0</p>
<p> Giza 77   166.0    160.0    154.0    148.0    142.0    139.0</p>
<p> Giza 75   140.0    134.0    128.0    122.0    116.0    113.0</p>
<p> Giza 85   131.0    125.0    119.0    113.0    107.0    104.0</p>
<p> Giza 83   127.0    121.0    115.0    109.0    103.0    100.0</p>
<p> Giza 80   127.0    121.0    115.0    109.0    103.0    100.0</p>
<p>Note - FG/EX = fully good/excellent, G/FG = good/fully good</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
